{
  "$schema": "elder-souls/viewpoints@1",
  "note": "W1-01 PROVINCE viewpoint set, APPENDED per HARNESS.md §6 (\"viewpoints may be added by amendment\"). It does not touch tools/harness/viewpoints.json: the twelve canonical poses are absolute and sit within 130 m of the world origin, the world origin is 250 m out in the Topal Bay, and changing a pose invalidates every cross-wave comparison that used it. Those twelve keep shooting W1-00's origin neighbourhood (the `showcase` cell, reached by the state `showcase_patch` and by every anchor state that sets `env.showcase`); these shoot the province. Capture with tools/world/province-shots.mjs, which teleports, streams the tiles in, and poses the camera directly.  W1-05 RECONCILIATION (wave 1): every viewpoint here carried `anchor: \"region_<name>\"` and not one of those thirteen states exists in game/data/states. That was not merely an unused field — tools/harness/shot.mjs:107 and shoot.mjs:157 both do `v.state || v.anchor` and hand it to loadState, where hOpt swallows the failure. So a shot taken through either tool loaded nothing, kept whatever state was already resident, and was then labelled with the anchor it had NOT been taken at. A silently wrong label on a picture is worse than a missing one, because a missing one gets fixed. The field is renamed to `region`, which is what it always meant: it is the `id` of a region in game/data/world/regions.json, and all thirteen resolve, and nothing loads it. Positioning is and always was `province.teleport`, honoured by tools/world/province-shots.mjs. If a per-region anchor state is ever authored, add `state:` alongside — do not put it back in `anchor`.",
  "capture": {
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "deviceScaleFactor": 1,
    "format": "png",
    "settleFrames": 24,
    "disableUI": true,
    "colorProfile": "srgb"
  },
